# --- secrets: NEVER commit ---
test-keys.env
*.env
!*.example.env

# --- nested git/bare repos ---
charon-rebuild-backup.git/

# --- ephemeral fleet runtime state (claims/submitted/done markers) ---
fleet/state/*
# ...except the persisted roadmap (canonical source for report.sh/handoff.sh).
!fleet/state/ROADMAP.tsv
# ...except the coverage-meta-gate rule registry (durable, git-tracked by design —
# consumed by fleet/checks/rule-coverage.sh; the §11 mechanized-coverage source of truth).
!fleet/state/RULE-REGISTRY.tsv
# ...except the REVIEWER-DOGFOOD-REDS ground-truth corpus (durable, git-tracked by
# design — see REDS-CORPUS.md's own OOB design note).
!fleet/state/REDS-CORPUS.md
# ...except the bidirectional rule-coverage audit register (RULE-SYNC-AUDIT
# ticket) — durable, derived from the sibling frameworks' inventories.
!fleet/state/RULE-SYNC-REGISTER.tsv
# ...except the config-drift source registry (CONFIG-SOURCES ticket) — local + gateway,
# durable; config-drift.sh reads this to detect provider siloing.
!fleet/state/CONFIG-SOURCES.tsv
# ...except the BENCH-PROVISIONAL-SCORING design of record (#20 — operator-led
# deep-dive 2026-07-16). Durable design artifact, sibling to PATH-C-DOGFOOD-EVAL
# / EVAL-TAXONOMY / EVAL-PIPELINE-DESIGN / S8-GRACEFUL-DEGRADE-DESIGN above;
# tracked so a build session / #26 rebase can read it without checking out a
# branch. (Other long-lived design docs in fleet/state/ are tracked; this
# exemption exists because the blanket `fleet/state/*` is otherwise more
# restrictive than the original design-doc pattern.)
!fleet/state/BENCH-PROVISIONAL-SCORING-DESIGN.md
# ...except the five durable artifacts owned by in-flight rig tickets. Landed AHEAD
# of those PRs deliberately: `.gitignore` is an anchor file, and four separate PRs
# (#97 #96 #93 #47) each appended their own negation here. Serialising them meant
# re-resolving the same conflict three times, and every merge invalidated the other
# branches' patch context. Landing all five negations up front dissolves the only
# contention edge in the open-PR set so the rest are file-disjoint.
!fleet/state/SSOT-REGISTRY.tsv
!fleet/state/REACHABILITY-AUDIT.md
!fleet/state/.reachability-allowlist
!fleet/state/provider-pricing-limits.tsv
!fleet/state/LAND-SH-POSTMORTEM.md
# ...and FREE-TIER-LIMITS.tsv (#116), which is currently tracked only because it was
# force-added; it had no negation line at all. Made explicit for consistency.
!fleet/state/FREE-TIER-LIMITS.tsv
# ...and the EVAL-REGISTRY tool-adoption source-of-record — a durable, append-only
# curated registry (sibling to REDS-CORPUS/RULE-SYNC-REGISTER above), referenced by the
# deep-dive eval docs and the tool-adoption sweep. Was living on-disk only (no negation);
# tracked now so the manager's land and every worktree carry it.
!fleet/state/EVAL-REGISTRY.md
# ...and the KSF linter-tools review — the durable eval that grounds the bandit/vulture
# adopt-vs-keep verdicts (product/stdlib scope vs rig CI scope). Was on-disk only; tracked
# now so the EVAL-REGISTRY bandit row's citation resolves in every checkout.
!fleet/state/KSF-LINTER-TOOLS-REVIEW.md

# --- KSF tool local runtime store (SQLite DB regenerated by the tool; NOT source) ---
.ksf/

# --- scratch / logs ---
*.log
fleet/logs/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
fleet/state/overnight/

# auto-gen REDS registry (regenerated by build-rig; never source-tracked)
fleet/reds.tsv

# runtime artifacts (regenerated; never source-tracked)
fleet/scorecard.v1.json
fleet/provider-exhaustion-ledger.tsv
fleet/model-scorecard.tsv
